              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  We found no NSF Certified for Sport, Informed Choice or Informed Sport listing for Premier shakes or powders, or for the new Muscle Milk shakes. Muscle Milk's Pro Series and Genuine powders are listed as NSF Certified for Sport by the brand and on Amazon. Tested athletes should confirm the exact product and flavor in the NSF database.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which is cheaper, Muscle Milk or Premier Protein?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Muscle Milk was cheaper per gram of protein in cartons at the Amazon prices we saw: about $1.68 per 25 g for the 26 g shake and $1.69 for Pro 33 g, against $1.86 for Premier 30 g. In 14 oz bottles Premier Ultimate was cheaper, about $2.23 against $2.55. Warehouse club sales can change the order.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Muscle Milk or Premier better for weight loss?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Premier is slightly better, because 30 g of protein in 160 calories with 4 g of carbs is the leanest ratio here. The standard Muscle Milk shake gives 26 g in the same calories with 11 g of carbs. The difference is modest, so either works in a calorie deficit. Talk to a doctor or dietitian before a large diet change.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

